WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.700
I'm beat.

3
00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.730
My body's burning up.

4
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.940
I'm still alive,
but at this rate,

5
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.040
I won't be for long.

6
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.550
Nobody's here.

7
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:34.590
An abandoned ship, full of
broken wood and scrap iron.

8
00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:38.060
Funny, huh? I fit right in.

9
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.100
I gotta do something about
this useless body of mine,

10
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.140
or I'm not gonna make it.

11
00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.670
Mwell, maybe.

12
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.890
So did you hear the news?

13
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.270
They're talking about it all over.

14
00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:44.280
"Tom's violent apprentice,
Cutty Flam, is dead."

15
00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.770
He was hit by the sea train.

16
00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.820
Iceburg, listen.

17
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.690
I know you can do it.

18
00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.820
You're the first
apprentice of Tom,

19
00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.020
the greatest shipwright
the world has ever known.

20
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:03.290
If anybody can do it, you can.

21
00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.190
Hey, Kokoro.

22
00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.830
One of these days
let's share a drink.

23
00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.440
You know, when we actually have something
to drink to.

24
00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.680
Yeah.

25
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.670
Tom, I won't let you down.

26
00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.390
I'll watch over your dreams.

27
00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.320
I'll protect everything.

28
00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:28.670
Not only this town but
these blueprints, as well!

29
00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.640
There's a visitor, sir.

30
00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:33.780
<b>Four Years Later</b>

31
00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.650
He said he's a friend from years back.

32
00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.350
Do you know anyone
named "Cutty Flam"?

33
00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.190
Franky?

34
00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:44.120
Shall I show him in, sir?

35
00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.160
No.

36
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.760
Turn him away.

37
00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.590
You sure picked a roundabout way of
meeting me.

38
00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.720
Mwell, maybe, but anyway,

39
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.420
what's up with that strange
looking body of yours?

40
00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:02.620
Screw you!

41
00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.360
The sea train mangled my body,
so in order to stay alive

42
00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.840
I rebuilt it using
some iron scraps.

43
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:08.970
But that's not the issue!

44
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.640
I've heard that your
company has been contracted

45
00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.910
to build ships for
the World Government!

46
00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.980
I won't tolerate you doing anything to
help them!

47
00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:15.940
How could you?

48
00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.950
They took Tom away!

49
00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.350
And the weapons that
caused the whole incident.

50
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.120
Have you forgotten
who made those?!

51
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:27.480
I'm sure you have plenty of
things you want to say to me,

52
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.290
but I have a few as well.

53
00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.760
I still haven't forgiven you.

54
00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.390
Four years isn't nearly enough time for
that.

55
00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.840
I'm surprised you
even have the nerve

56
00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.210
to show your face around
here after what happened!

57
00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.180
What'd you say?!

58
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.180
The government told me

59
00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.380
that you died in an
accident on the railway.

60
00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.980
You never came back so
I believed it to be true.

61
00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.410
Even if Tom forgave you,
remember this:

62
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.250
It doesn't mean for a second that I'm
going to.

63
00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.790
What's with all the secrecy?

64
00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.520
Something going on?

65
00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.840
Hey, what're these?

66
00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.630
The blueprints for that old battleship?

67
00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.260
Don't call yourself Cutty Flam anymore.

68
00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:08.700
It's only a matter of time

69
00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.640
before the
government targets me.

70
00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.470
Now listen carefully.

71
00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.380
I want you to take these and leave this
island, Franky.

72
00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:17.760
Why should I?

73
00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.680
The "Cutty Flam" from
Tom's Workers is dead.

74
00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.840
As long as you don't
use that name anymore,

75
00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.730
then there'll be no
connection between us.

76
00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.570
Additionally, if you
leave the island,

77
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.870
the whereabouts of the
blueprints will vanish.

78
00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.340
Hey, hold on a second!

79
00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.140
What happens if the
government comes after you

80
00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:34.820
and you don't have them?!

81
00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.490
I've said what I came to say.

82
00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:37.380
What the...?

83
00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.520
Hey, Iceburg!

84
00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.180
We shouldn't see each other again.

85
00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.420
Wait! Hold on!

86
00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:43.590
Listen to me.

87
00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.830
Do you want to end up the same way that
Tom did?

88
00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.490
Hang on to the blueprints.

89
00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.360
If you're threatened
and your life is in danger,

90
00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.470
just hand them over!

91
00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.400
And if you don't wanna do that,

92
00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.240
you can burn them
right before their eyes!

93
00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.210
If you were me, would you do that?

94
00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.220
Tom had achieved so many wonderful things.

95
00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.220
But he gave up everything

96
00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.180
to keep these blueprints
hidden from the world.

97
00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.920
As long as the risk remains
that a woman named Nico Robin

98
00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.750
can figure out how to restore
the weapon then the world

99
00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:14.460
needs these blueprints
to be able to fight back!

100
00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.320
If I continue to keep them
with me even if they

101
00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.440
threaten my life, I won't hand
them over to the government!

102
00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.210
Are you sure?

103
00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.940
You know me... what if
I decide to build it?

104
00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.280
Do you really think that you can trust me?

105
00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.070
I'm giving them to you.

106
00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.510
Doesn't that answer your question?

107
00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.450
We never change, do we?

108
00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.850
Every time we meet
face to face,

109
00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.260
we yell and argue
with each other.

110
00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:42.530
I won't forgive you, and you may
feel the same way about me, too.

111
00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:48.940
Franky, I'm, I'm really...

112
00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:52.820
I'm so glad that
you're still alive.

113
00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.160
You listen to me!

114
00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.900
I'm not gonna leave this island!

115
00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.900
You got that, Ice-for-brains?!

116
00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.870
I'm gonna do whatever the hell I wanna do!

117
00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.570
You think I'm gonna do what you tell me?

118
00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:10.580
I'd rather die!

119
00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.680
Understand?!

120
00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.820
Dammit, Flunky!

121
00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:23.210
<b>Bingo</b>

122
00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.840
We've heard that Tom was
an excellent craftsman

123
00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:28.110
and a creative
genius but he was also

124
00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:31.040
an uncontrollable fishman
with superhuman strength.

125
00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.080
When we ask the
citizens here about him,

126
00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.580
they don't really
have much to say.

127
00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:36.880
It must be difficult to

128
00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:39.120
apprentice under
a man like that.

129
00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.950
Right, Cutty Flam?

130
00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.990
That ridiculous question
doesn't even deserve a reply.

131
00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.590
You Government goons
are all piles of crap!

132
00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.030
Easy, easy!

133
00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.200
During that incident,
more than 100 people,

134
00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.960
including Marines
and Navy officers,

135
00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.030
were severely injured
here in Water Seven.

136
00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.140
And the culprit behind it was you.

137
00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:58.800
Causing the World Government

138
00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:01.570
that much trouble
is a serious crime.

139
00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:03.060
But because you were
confirmed dead

140
00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.400
in a sea train accident
later that same day,

141
00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:08.580
all of the charges against
you were annulled.

142
00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.550
Since you're
actually still alive,

143
00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.610
you'll be taken to
Enies Lobby as a criminal.

144
00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.650
There, you can take your time

145
00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.450
answering this one
simple question.

146
00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.050
Where are the secret blueprints

147
00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:21.460
for the ancient weapon
known as Pluton?

148
00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.070
Now, Blueno.

149
00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:27.960
Right, I was just able
to get a connection.

150
00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.440
When I reported
our latest findings

151
00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:33.180
on this case to our superior,
he said that he wanted to

152
00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.210
speak with you directly
and immediately.

153
00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.180
Superior, huh?

154
00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.680
All right, Chief. Go ahead.

155
00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.510
Hot! Hot! Ouch, ouch, ouch!

156
00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.250
I spilled coffee all over myself!

157
00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:48.260
Dammit! Stupid coffee!

158
00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.220
What the heck?

159
00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:56.260
So, you're still alive.
Greetings Cutty Flam.

160
00:08:55.850 --> 00:09:02.730
<b>Command Center
Enies Lobby</b>

161
00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.490
Long time no see.

162
00:08:58.520 --> 00:08:59.990
It's hard to believe you

163
00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:03.260
somehow managed to
survive the "accident."

164
00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:07.150
Hard to believe.
But good news, nonetheless.

165
00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.260
For the past eight years,
every time my scars hurt,

166
00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.690
I was tormented by
an unquenchable anger

167
00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.560
that I couldn't take the
proper vengeance I deserved.

168
00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.160
Because the criminal responsible

169
00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.100
for those scars
was dead, you see.

170
00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.670
I said who in
the hell are you?

171
00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.590
Don't you remember me?

172
00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:32.390
I'm the man from
Cipher Pol Number 5

173
00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:35.390
that arrested Tom's Workers
when I caught them red-handed

174
00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:38.770
<b>Chief Spandam
Cipher Pol No. 9</b>

175
00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.300
for savagely attacking the
Judicial Ship 8 years ago!

176
00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:41.760
You're that Spanda
guy, aren't you?!

177
00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:44.470
Spandam!

178
00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:45.440
You're missing the M!

179
00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.440
But I'll have plenty
of time to drill that

180
00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.080
into your head once
you arrive at Enies Lobby!

181
00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.480
Make it quick, men.

182
00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.550
I'm simply dying to teach
that criminal a lesson!

183
00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.710
Damned stupid lamp!

184
00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:06.560
Tie him up.

185
00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:13.200
Hey punk!
Watch those hands!

186
00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:14.360
Come on.

187
00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.580
Let him go!

188
00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.320
Come back here, you bastards!

189
00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:36.060
Uh. I'm sorry.

190
00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.220
Hey!

191
00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.560
If you're not gonna help,
then don't get my hopes up!

192
00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.560
Wait, I know you, don't I?

193
00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.500
You're part of the Straw Hat crew.

194
00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:54.470
<b>Headquarters
Galley-La Company</b>

195
00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.470
No good!
The wind is too strong!

196
00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:54.470
It's getting worse!

197
00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:58.620
If Iceburg's in there,
we gotta get him out now!

198
00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.200
Iceburg!

199
00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.950
Paulie!

200
00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:30.120
Nami! Oh no, I have to
treat her right away.

201
00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.550
If can just...

202
00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.030
Hurry!
They need first aid!

203
00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:45.660
They're burned all over!

204
00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:46.560
Hey!

205
00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.900
What're we gonna do
with this reindeer?!

206
00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:48.800
Help him!

207
00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:50.100
He saved their lives!

208
00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.300
Y-You're right.

209
00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:55.360
Hey! Someone gimme a hand!

210
00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.840
Oh boy.

211
00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:04.120
That's just sad.

212
00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.980
So what you're saying is
that you left the Straw Hats,

213
00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:12.950
but you haven't given
up your life of crime.

214
00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:15.320
What a shame.

215
00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:17.790
If you're a pirate, you're coming with us.

216
00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:18.590
Kalifa.

217
00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.190
Got it.

218
00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:24.720
And as for this ship.

219
00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:28.350
You still haven't disposed of it?

220
00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:29.820
Stay away!

221
00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.720
Don't you dare touch her!

222
00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:46.210
Are you listening to me?!
What're you doing?!

223
00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.610
Even if it was only
a temporary disguise,

224
00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:51.080
we are still respected
as shipwrights.

225
00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:58.520
When we say your
ship's done for

226
00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.990
then you would do
well to listen to us.

227
00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:04.230
What do you care?!
It's not even your ship!

228
00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.690
I can do whatever I want with it!

229
00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.190
This lever releases the water,
right?

230
00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:12.980
Cut it out! That's not
funny, damn it! Hey!

231
00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:28.190
No, stop it!
Don't let her fall!

232
00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.970
Don't worry.

233
00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:44.890
I'll carry everyone for a little bit
longer.

234
00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:06.660
Merry!

235
00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:11.540
<b>Headquarters
Galley-La Company</b>

236
00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:15.840
Get back!

237
00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.600
Run away!

238
00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.310
Come on!

239
00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.510
You idiot! Run!

240
00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:31.350
Dammit! Isn't there
anything we can do?!

241
00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:41.390
Look! Mr. Iceburg's awake!

242
00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.390
All right! He's safe!

243
00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:46.030
I knew he'd make it!

244
00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.450
That reindeer saved his life!

245
00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:51.770
Are you sure?

246
00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:54.300
I thought it belonged
to the Straw Hats.

247
00:14:58.780 --> 00:14:59.650
Hey! Look!

248
00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:04.790
This woman's from the Straw Hats,
too!

249
00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.640
So what now?

250
00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:09.010
Do you think maybe we should tie her up
and question her?

251
00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.910
I dunno, she's just a
girl and she's hurt, too.

252
00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:14.680
I know, but...

253
00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.550
Whoa!

254
00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.650
You shouldn't be
moving yet, Mr. Iceburg!

255
00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:24.410
Sorry men but I need a
little space, right now.

256
00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.280
That is to say, I want to speak to this
woman in private.

257
00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.340
Wonder what those two are talking about.

258
00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.670
Beats me.

259
00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.630
What was that for?!

260
00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:47.220
Stop standing there
and gimme a hand!

261
00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.820
I know Iceburg and
Paulie are safe,

262
00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:51.690
but the rest of the foremen
might still be trapped inside!

263
00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.450
Yeah, he's right!

264
00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:53.860
Let's go.

265
00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:58.560
Oh, uh. Yeah, sorry!

266
00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:02.770
Mmwell, first off
I must apologize.

267
00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:06.360
I falsely accused your entire crew.

268
00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:09.900
I'll try to clear that up soon.

269
00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.780
But for now, I want to talk about Nico
Robin.

270
00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.940
What do you know?

271
00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:19.480
When you first came to Water Seven,
did she start acting strangely?

272
00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:20.980
Yeah, she did.

273
00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:24.420
She went into town that day and then never
came back.

274
00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:28.290
By the next morning she
was the prime suspect

275
00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:29.930
in your attempted murder.

276
00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.570
When Sanji and Chopper
finally saw her again,

277
00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.930
she said this was goodbye

278
00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:37.160
and wouldn't be a part
of the crew anymore.

279
00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:39.760
Of course, none of that
made any sense to us

280
00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.930
so we decided to break
into your mansion,

281
00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.500
in hopes that we'd
be able to see her

282
00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:46.470
one more time and
find out the truth.

283
00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.820
I did it to make my wish come true.

284
00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:52.070
One that can't happen as
long as we're together,

285
00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.680
if you can't accept
that, I'm sorry.

286
00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:57.380
What kind of wish
would force her

287
00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:00.580
to give up all of her friends?

288
00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:03.080
I think I know the answer, actually.

289
00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.520
This probably started
shortly after you lost sight

290
00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:12.560
of her for the first time.

291
00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:14.640
The government had
begun its operation

292
00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.740
the moment she arrived.

293
00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.470
In other words,
there's a good reason

294
00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.410
why your friend
did what she did.

295
00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:24.840
But before I go
into the details,

296
00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:27.010
I want you to understand
that both Nico Robin

297
00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.580
and I have the means to
revive an ancient weapon

298
00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.700
that is capable of
destroying the entire world.

299
00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:34.450
Huh? A weapon?

300
00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:35.960
That's right.

301
00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.640
Puru-puru. Puru-puru. Click.

302
00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:39.740
It's me.

303
00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.640
We've hit a snag in the plan.

304
00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:44.780
Everyone head to the bedroom immediately.

305
00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:49.550
Don't shoot Iceburg yet.

306
00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.780
Do you understand now?

307
00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.890
The blueprints that
they found are fake!

308
00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.580
I don't care.

309
00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.420
I would rather die
than hand over

310
00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:02.450
that information to
the government.

311
00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.050
But now it's not that simple.

312
00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.220
If you've decided that
you're going to help them

313
00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.600
and you're searching for
the Poneglyphs yourself.

314
00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:13.230
Then I have to do
everything I can to stop you!

315
00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:14.840
I understand your concern,

316
00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.640
but I'm only studying
the poneglyphs

317
00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.600
to learn more about the
history of the world.

318
00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:21.780
I don't care about the weapon.

319
00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.640
You have to take responsibility!

320
00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:28.400
I told you this would happen.

321
00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:31.570
But you don't listen.

322
00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:35.290
Franky, even if you
weren't trying to.

323
00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:37.590
Weapons are made
to hurt people.

324
00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:43.600
Whether you want them to or not,
they can hurt your friends.

325
00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:45.670
Even if you don't have
malicious intent,

326
00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.170
your actions can
still hurt people!

327
00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:51.110
If your curiosity for history
leads to the destruction

328
00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.350
of the world then you're
better off dying

329
00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:56.480
right here and right
now, Nico Robin!

330
00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:00.350
Even after seeing what
happened to the devils of Ohara,

331
00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:03.760
you still want to
walk this path?!

332
00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:06.690
You don't know a damned
thing about Ohara!

333
00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:09.310
You have no idea how
much the World Government

334
00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.340
has warped my life,
do you hear me?

335
00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:16.340
If you hate the government
so much then why help them?!

336
00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:24.000
Because I have a wish that I would
sacrifice anything for.

337
00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:31.580
When I came to this town,

338
00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:34.450
CP9 presented me
with two conditions.

339
00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.880
The first was to pin
your assassination

340
00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:39.750
on the Straw Hats
and leave their crew.

341
00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.490
The second was to turn
myself over to the government

342
00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.700
and follow their every
order without question.

343
00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:48.870
You realize, they
won't let you live.

344
00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:51.140
You escaped them for 20 years.

345
00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:55.110
Why would you agree to something like that
now?

346
00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:59.000
In this particular instance,
CP9 has been given

347
00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:02.610
permission to activate a Buster
Call against the Straw Hats.

348
00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.380
A Buster Call?

349
00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.340
It's an emergency order that
summons five vice admirals

350
00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:12.510
and ten battleships
to the same location.

351
00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:14.310
No matter how strong you are,

352
00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:19.610
no one can survive a full-scale
military attack of that caliber.

353
00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:22.670
Under normal circumstances,
only the three admirals

354
00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.870
and the head of the
navy, the fleet admiral,

355
00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.400
are allowed to exercise
that kind of authority.

356
00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:30.580
However, this is a special case.

357
00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:32.540
Just this once,

358
00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:37.480
Admiral Aokiji has given CP9
the right to make the call.

359
00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:39.000
When I heard his name, I surrendered.

360
00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.300
If I hadn't agreed to
their conditions, then me

361
00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.340
and the rest of the Straw Hats
would've been annihilated.

362
00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.640
For the past 20 years I've been
able to run away and survive,

363
00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.850
no matter what the
circumstance but that's only

364
00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:54.320
because I had nothing to
protect because I was willing

365
00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.720
to betray others and
use them as a shield.

366
00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:57.890
But not now.

367
00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:04.000
For the first time in all
these years I can't do that.

368
00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.500
They picked up the
life I gave up on,

369
00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:11.480
returned the heart I lost
and continued the dreams

370
00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.850
that I no longer believed in.

371
00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.780
Even after all I've done,

372
00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:20.550
I've found friends who
will still believe in me.

373
00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:25.610
I see but then
what is your wish?

374
00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:29.820
That excluding me all of
the other Straw Hat pirates

375
00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:32.520
will be allowed to
leave this island safely!

376
00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:36.020
And as long as
you have that,

377
00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:39.150
you don't care what happens to
you of the rest of the world?!

378
00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:41.110
I don't.

379
00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:44.710
I've heard all I can take.

380
00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:54.290
In the end, I couldn't pull the trigger.

381
00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:03.880
She was willing to
sacrifice the lives

382
00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:06.150
of everyone in this
world, even her own.

383
00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:10.790
As long as she could
save the six of you.

384
00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:12.860
She was protecting us.

385
00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:14.630
As much as I hate to admit it,

386
00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:16.720
I have no right
to criticize her.

387
00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:20.660
If they find the blueprints now,
it's all my fault.

388
00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:27.990
Hey! What's wrong?

389
00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:33.570
I'm happy, that's all.

390
00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:35.840
I was so worried.

391
00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:38.210
I didn't want to
believe she betrayed us.

392
00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:42.960
I gotta find everyone
else and let them know!

393
00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:44.200
Thank you, Iceburg!

394
00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:46.280
Hold on! What are you
going to do now?

395
00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:49.050
The Straw Hats have already lost to CP9!

396
00:22:49.070 --> 00:22:50.800
What do you mean we lost?

397
00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:52.940
We haven't even started fighting yet!

398
00:22:53.020 --> 00:22:56.320
We wouldn't be here right now if we gave
up that easy.

399
00:22:56.360 --> 00:22:58.890
Luffy will get Robin back, you'll see.

400
00:22:58.950 --> 00:23:01.850
We just needed motivation, that's all.

401
00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:05.720
Now that we know
Robin needs saving.

402
00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:08.930
There's no limit to
what we can accomplish!

403
00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:15.100
Chopper! Great news!

404
00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:18.630
C'mon Chopper, wake up!
We have to find everyone!

405
00:23:19.270 --> 00:23:20.400
You can sleep
when you're dead.

406
00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:25.260
Wake up! Wake up!

407
00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:27.010
Wake up!

408
00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:28.680
Hey, Chopper.

409
00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:30.250
Go meet up with
Luffy and the others

410
00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:33.020
and tell them everything that
happened between us and Robin.

411
00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:34.950
I don't want you to leave out a single
word.

412
00:23:34.980 --> 00:23:36.890
Sure.

413
00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:39.460
As for me, let's just say I have a plan.

414
00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:43.460
I'll try to be careful.
We'll meet up later.

415
00:23:47.130 --> 00:23:48.800
Something wrong?

416
00:23:48.830 --> 00:23:53.670
Do you think Robin
doesn't like us anymore?

417
00:23:58.650 --> 00:23:59.260
Chopper.

418
00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:01.480
Let me share a
secret with you.

419
00:24:04.210 --> 00:24:05.630
When a woman tells a lie...

420
00:24:07.430 --> 00:24:09.340
...a real man forgives her.

421
00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:16.600
<b>Blue Station
Water Seven</b>

422
00:24:12.190 --> 00:24:14.130
Attention all
passengers boarding

423
00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.500
today's final service
to Enies Lobby.

424
00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:18.800
Due to the current water level,
we will be departing

425
00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:20.710
from the platform
on the second floor.

426
00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:24.010
Boarding time is 11:00 PM.

427
00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:25.210
Let's go see who they are!

428
00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:25.990
Yeah!

429
00:24:29.710 --> 00:24:32.640
This is a top-secret
operation we're running here.

430
00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:34.910
The agents must board in private.

431
00:24:34.960 --> 00:24:36.160
– No fair.
– No fair.

432
00:24:43.040 --> 00:24:46.170
How considerate of you to finally turn
yourself in.

433
00:24:46.200 --> 00:24:48.870
20 years is a
long time to run.

434
00:25:01.650 --> 00:25:02.900
Bingo.
